{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CoherentCollapseSinhCosh","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.CoherentCollapseSinhCosh","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.coherent_vs_observe_last","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.coherent_vs_observe_last","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CoherentCollapseSinhCosh.lean#L74-L85","doc":"**Coherent collapse vs observe-last.** For two blocks whose bar-odd parts have\nopposite chirality (`+s`, `-s` — the rotation/growth split, PR #1742), the\n**coherent** sum (extract *after* summing) is `(y - y')·s`, which **nulls** at\nequal weights; the **observe-last** sum (`|·|` per block, *then* sum) is\n`(y + y')·s`, which **survives**. This is the algebraic core of the\nowner-confirmed coherent-collapse cancellation (the `c_3`-carrying `sinh` is\nexactly what the coherent sum can null while the incoherent sum keeps). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.bracket_two_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.bracket_two_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CoherentCollapseSinhCosh.lean#L69-L72","doc":"`[2]_q` is **bar-EVEN**: `[2]_q(-η) = [2]_q(η)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hecke_h_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hecke_h_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CoherentCollapseSinhCosh.lean#L64-L67","doc":"`h` is **bar-ODD**: under the Lusztig bar `η ↦ -η`, `h(-η) = -h(η)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.std_char_sigma1_eq_two_sinh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.std_char_sigma1_eq_two_sinh","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CoherentCollapseSinhCosh.lean#L58-L62","doc":"The standard-rep `(2,1)` character of one crossing `σ_1` is the sum of its two\nHecke eigenvalues `q + (-q⁻¹) = q - q⁻¹ = 2 sinh η` — **pure bar-odd**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.eigenvalue_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.eigenvalue_neg","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CoherentCollapseSinhCosh.lean#L54-L56","doc":"The inverse eigenvalue: `q⁻¹ = exp(-η) = cosh η - sinh η`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.eigenvalue_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.eigenvalue_pos","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CoherentCollapseSinhCosh.lean#L50-L52","doc":"The positive Hecke eigenvalue: `q = exp η = cosh η + sinh η`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.bracket_two_eq_two_cosh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.bracket_two_eq_two_cosh","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CoherentCollapseSinhCosh.lean#L44-L48","doc":"The **bar-EVEN** generator `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` equals `2 cosh η`\n(the `c_2` sector generator). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hecke_h_eq_two_sinh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hecke_h_eq_two_sinh","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CoherentCollapseSinhCosh.lean#L38-L42","doc":"The **bar-ODD** Hecke generator `h = q - q⁻¹` equals `2 sinh η` at `q = exp η`\n(the `c_3` sector generator). ","signatureChunk":0}]}